menu "Zigbee Router (zb_router)"

    config ZB_ROUTER_CHANNEL
        int "Zigbee channel (0 = scan all channels 11-26)"
        range 0 26
        default 0
        help
            The 802.15.4 channel network steering is allowed to use.

            0 scans every Zigbee channel (11-26). Any value 11-26 pins steering
            to that single channel; set it to your coordinator's channel (ZHA
            shows it under the Zigbee network settings). Values 1-10 are not
            Zigbee channels and fail the build.

            Pinning the channel alone is NOT enough to avoid joining a
            neighbor's network on the same channel; also set the extended PAN
            ID below.

    config ZB_ROUTER_EXT_PAN_ID
        string "Extended PAN ID to join (16 hex chars, 0 = any network)"
        default "0000000000000000"
        help
            The extended PAN ID (EPID) of the network this device may join,
            as 16 hex characters, big-endian, i.e. in the same byte order ZHA
            displays it. Colons are allowed and ignored, so
            "0123456789abcdef" and "01:23:45:67:89:ab:cd:ef" are equivalent.

            All zeros means "any network": steering associates with the first
            network in range that permits joining, which may not be yours.
            Setting your coordinator's EPID makes steering associate only with
            that network. The EPID is public beacon data, not a secret.

            A malformed value makes zb_router_start() fail with
            ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG rather than silently falling back to
            "any network".

    config ZB_ROUTER_MAX_CHILDREN
        int "Maximum joined children"
        range 1 64
        default 10
        help
            Router capacity for child devices (end devices that pick this
            router as parent). The esp-zigbee-sdk examples use 10.

    config ZB_ROUTER_RETRY_DELAY_MS
        int "Commissioning retry delay (ms)"
        range 100 600000
        default 1000
        help
            Delay before re-running a failed BDB initialization or network
            steering attempt. Steering retries forever until a join succeeds.

    config ZB_ROUTER_TASK_STACK_SIZE
        int "Zigbee task stack size (bytes)"
        range 3072 32768
        default 4096
        help
            Stack of the task running the Zigbee stack main loop. The
            endpoint-registration callback, the signal hook and the joined
            callback all run on this task; raise it if they need more stack.

    config ZB_ROUTER_TASK_PRIORITY
        int "Zigbee task priority"
        range 1 24
        default 5

    choice ZB_ROUTER_ANTENNA
        prompt "RF antenna switch"
        default ZB_ROUTER_ANTENNA_NONE
        help
            Some boards route the radio through an RF switch that must be
            enabled (and an antenna selected) before the radio starts.

            The Seeed XIAO ESP32-C6 has one: GPIO3 enables the RF switch
            (driven LOW) and GPIO14 selects the antenna (LOW = built-in
            ceramic, HIGH = external u.FL). Pick one of the XIAO options on
            that board and keep GPIO3/GPIO14 free for antenna control.

            Leave "None" on any other board: the XIAO options drive GPIO3 and
            GPIO14 as outputs, which may clash with other hardware.

        config ZB_ROUTER_ANTENNA_NONE
            bool "None (no RF switch on this board)"

        config ZB_ROUTER_ANTENNA_XIAO_ONBOARD
            bool "XIAO ESP32-C6: built-in ceramic antenna"
            depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32C6

        config ZB_ROUTER_ANTENNA_XIAO_EXTERNAL
            bool "XIAO ESP32-C6: external u.FL antenna"
            depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32C6
    endchoice

endmenu
